`rewind` does not restore prior state: it forks a sibling branch from the anchor and continues forward from a model-generated summary.

Operations (set `action`):
  • 'anchor', name='<milestone-name>': label the current point. Anchor at the start of a stage you'll summarize (e.g. 'impl-start').
  • 'rewind', rewindTo='<existing>', newLabel='<new>': collapse work between rewindTo and the current leaf into a branch_summary labeled newLabel, so rewinds can chain.
  • 'list': show all anchors on the active branch, oldest first, with cumulative context % at each.
  • 'pin', kind='sub-goal'|'decision'|'fact'|'file'|'steering', text='<what to keep>': record a durable item that survives folds; `list` shows them. 'file' takes path+why instead of text; 'steering' belongs to an anchor (scopeAnchor, default newest). Refused when the user disabled the continuity ledger (continuity.capture=false).

`name` (anchor) and `newLabel` (rewind) write into one shared anchor namespace: labels are unique on the active branch — both actions refuse a name that already exists — and everything written there is addressable as a future `rewindTo`. Avoid the reserved `anchor:` prefix.","parameters":{"type":"object","required":["action"],"properties":{"action":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string","const":"anchor"},{"type":"string","const":"rewind"},{"type":"string","const":"list"},{"type":"string","const":"pin"}],"description":"Which operation to perform."},"name":{"type":"string","description":"Required when action='anchor'. Kebab-case milestone label, max 40 chars."},"rewindTo":{"type":"string","description":"Required when action='rewind'. Kebab-case name of an existing anchor on the active branch to rewind to."},"newLabel":{"type":"string","description":"Required when action='rewind'. Kebab-case label for the resulting branch_summary entry; reusable as a future rewindTo."},"summaryFocus":{"type":"string","description":"Required when action='rewind'; ≥20 chars after trim. Encode: (1) the user's most recent instruction verbatim, (2) what's done in the collapsed segment, (3) what's left to do as a next action; if the user authorized continuing, name the next work item, not a report or wrap-up."},"kind":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string","const":"sub-goal"},{"type":"string","const":"decision"},{"type":"string","const":"fact"},{"type":"string","const":"file"},{"type":"string","const":"steering"}],"description":"Required when action='pin'. Your sub-goal, a decision you made, a key fact, a file pointer, or steering that lapses when its anchor is folded."},"text":{"type":"string","description":"Required when action='pin' unless kind='file'. What to remember, max 500 chars."},"path":{"type":"string","description":"Required when action='pin' and kind='file'. File path."},"lines":{"type":"string","description":"Optional with kind='file': N or N-M."},"why":{"type":"string","description":"Required when action='pin' and kind='file'. Why the file matters."},"scopeAnchor":{"type":"string","description":"Anchor name for kind='steering' (default: newest anchor); optional for 'sub-goal'."}}},"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_acceptance_fixture","description":"Read page 1 or 2 of the separate synthetic schema-inventory dataset.","parameters":{"type":"object","required":["page"],"properties":{"page":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"maximum":2}}},"strict":false}],"reasoning":{"effort":"none"}}

